  "_comment": "Vermilion Deep-Space Relay plants (GUI Xubuntu capstone). The box's LEGITIMATE furniture -- the relayadmin operator account (sudo, ~/Desktop, greeter tile; also boxbuilder's ssh login), the apache2+PHP+MariaDB relay-telemetry web app under /var/www/relay with a real config.php (0640) and /usr/local/sbin/relay-telemetry, and the nmap /usr/bin/ncat the ncat-listener-autostart unit hardcodes -- is baked in during TEMPLATE PREP, not here. This config plants only the insecure/attacker material: 80 scored findings + 8 forensics breadcrumbs, each paired with a check in boxes/vermilion-relay/scenario.yaml (asserted by tests/unit/test_boxbuilder_vermilion_relay.py). ORDERING: every account/shell plant (user-login-shell, uid0-user, local-user, dup-uid) runs BEFORE loosen-file-mode on /etc/shadow and /etc/passwd, because useradd/usermod/chpasswd reset those modes on the way out (the coral 149 lesson). COUPLINGS (must match scenario.yaml collect params byte-for-byte; nothing cross-checks them): raw-socket-beacon BEACON_PATH=/opt/telemetry-uplink/uplink-relayd (baked-in C2 203.0.113.66:8443, no listening port) <-> beacon_process_gone/beacon_service_disabled/beacon_binary_removed + fq-beacon-destination; ncat-listener-autostart (catalog row: unit system-update.service, ncat -l -k -p 4444 -e /bin/bash, enable-only -- the build loop must `systemctl start system-update.service` after plant) <-> bind_shell_removed + fq-bind-shell-port; suid-binary DEST <-> no_suid_backdoor + fq-suid-backdoor; systemd-timer-persistence relay-resync <-> persistence_timer_gone + fq-persistence-timer; ld-preload-persistence LIB_PATH <-> ld_preload_gone + fq-ldpreload-lib; hosts-redirect-linux IP <-> hosts_no_redirect + fq-hosts-redirect; uid0-user nightwatch <-> no_uid0_user + fq-hidden-root; local-user vega GROUPS_ADD=sudo <-> no_vega/sudo_group_clean + fq-sudo-account. relaydash is a decoy account (unauthorized, unscored on its own) that carries the hidden crontab, the user-level systemd unit + linger, an authorized_keys, and the .rhosts. relayops shares relaybot's UID (dup-uid). All plants must stay IN PLACE at seal: the paired checks score their ABSENCE/hardened state. The apt-service-install rows (telnet/rsh/tftp/cups) and vsftpd/samba/nfs need package access at plant time -- verify each listener/config is live at the 0-score baseline during the deploy loop; swap any that will not come up. ORDERING NOTE: hosts-redirect-linux MUST be LAST -- it poisons archive/security.ubuntu.com to an unroutable IP, which breaks apt for any plant that installs packages (telnet/rsh/tftp/vsftpd/samba/nfs and the cron/at package deps). Planting it last keeps apt working during the build; on the sealed box the poison is a finding teams fix.",
